#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-AD0261 expect=violation domain=ADAE
# Rule:Description: Raise an error when AEDECOD is not present in an ADVERSE EVENT sub-class OCCDS dataset (e.g., ADAE).
#note "Precedence pin, INVERTED BY FIX #154. structure=/subclass= is the DECLARED tier, and corej.defineFirst now defaults to TRUE (decision D21-remainder), so the declaration BEATS a confident contradicting column detection: PARAMCD/AVAL detect BASIC DATA STRUCTURE, the declaration says OCCURRENCE DATA STRUCTURE / ADVERSE EVENT, and the declaration wins -- exactly what a contradicting Define-XML def:Class now does. Before Fix #154 this same scenario was expect=skipped (file name -skipped-ADAE-declaration-loses-to-columns.cdt). The argument for the flip: reclassifying by columns HIDES a defect -- a declaration that disagrees with the data is itself a conformance finding, and an engine must report it rather than quietly re-declare on the sponsor's behalf. The -Dcorej.defineFirst=false half is pinned in ScenarioDeclaredScopeProviderTest, which can toggle the property. Neuter by reverting AdamDataStructureDetector.defineFirstPreference() to Boolean.getBoolean: the columns win again, the rule is skipped, and this scenario goes red."
# The #define block is the mandatory carrier for a structure=/subclass= declaration — see
# README-CDT.md, "ADaM structure / subclass".
#define standard=adamig version=1-3
#expectViolationCount 1
dataset ADAE structure=OCCDS subclass=AE
col STUDYID type=Char
col PARAMCD type=Char
col AVAL type=Num
---
CDISCPILOT01 | HEIGHT | 170
---
